Theorem IC-2: ParamContract initialization at most-optimistic state

  Preconditions:
    - IC-1 has decomposed the CallGraph into SCCs in forward
      topological order (callees before callers) per
      Annex E §AIMS IC-1 + sec-7 PL-1a; the shipped
      ori_arc::aims::interprocedural::analyze_program iterates
      that list before any per-function step runs
    - SCC fixpoint iteration is BOTTOM-UP over the partial order
      `≤` defined componentwise on each lattice dimension; per
      Annex E §AIMS.8 L-4 partial order `a ≤ b ⟺ a ⊔ b = b`
    - IC-3 (proven separately) provides the componentwise join
      operator used to PROMOTE param contracts toward conservative
      across call sites; IC-2 fixes only the INITIAL state, before
      any join has fired
    - IC-2 type signature (per Interprocedural.proof lines 21-25):
        initial_param_contract : Unit -> ParamContract
      whose output is the bottom of the per-parameter sub-lattice
      across every dimension simultaneously
    - Spec statement (Annex E §AIMS IC-2): "Each parameter
      initializes most optimistic: (Borrowed, Dead, Absent,
      BlockLocal, Unique, may_share=false). Fixpoint promotes
      toward conservative."
    - Shipped engine: `ParamContract::OPTIMISTIC` const at
      compiler/ori_arc/src/aims/contract/mod.rs:368
      lines 368-386; consumed by IC-2 seeding inside
      ori_arc::aims::interprocedural::analyze_program at the
      SCC-entry point before backward dataflow runs
    - Target-vs-shipped axis carve-out (per Annex E §AIMS
      "Target-only / partially-shipped subsystems" top-of-file):
      spec ParamContract removed `may_escape` (derived from
      Locality dimension); shipped ParamContract retains
      `may_escape` + `locality_bound` as parallel fields. IC-2
      proof discharges the 5-dim spec statement; shipped struct
      carries 5 spec dims + 1 target-vs-shipped legacy field
      (`may_escape: false`) + 3 IC-4 return-flow fields
      (`transfers_through_return: false`, `return_alias: None`,
      `return_payload_contains_param: false`) that initialize to
      their own bottoms

  Soundness property:
    Forall ParamContract instance pc emitted as the SCC fixpoint
    seed for any parameter of any function in any SCC.
      pc = initial_param_contract() SHALL hold along five
      dimensions enumerated by spec Annex E §AIMS IC-2:

      (P1) Access dimension bottom:
        pc.access = AccessClass::Borrowed
        (per Annex E §AIMS §3.1: `Borrowed < Owned`; Borrowed
        is the unique minimum element of the Access lattice).

      (P2) Consumption dimension bottom:
        pc.consumption = Consumption::Dead
        (per Annex E §AIMS.2:
        `Dead < Linear < Affine < Unrestricted`;
        Dead is the unique minimum element of the Consumption
        lattice).

      (P3) Cardinality dimension bottom:
        pc.cardinality = Cardinality::Absent
        (per Annex E §AIMS.3:
        `Absent < Once < Many`; Absent is the unique minimum
        element of the Cardinality lattice).

      (P4) Locality dimension bottom:
        pc.locality_bound = Locality::BlockLocal
        (per Annex E §AIMS.5:
        `BlockLocal < FunctionLocal < ArgEscaping < HeapEscaping
        < Unknown`; BlockLocal is the unique minimum element of
        the Locality lattice).

      (P5) Uniqueness dimension bottom:
        pc.uniqueness = Uniqueness::Unique
        (per Annex E §AIMS.4:
        `Unique < MaybeShared < Shared`; Unique is the unique
        minimum element of the Uniqueness lattice).

      (P6) Per-parameter sharing flag bottom:
        pc.may_share = false
        (per Annex E §AIMS IC-3: `may_share` is joined by
        OR across call sites; `false` is the OR-identity, hence
        the unique minimum element of the boolean
        sub-lattice).

      Conjunction over (P1)..(P6) IS the spec statement
      "(Borrowed, Dead, Absent, BlockLocal, Unique,
      may_share=false)".

  Proof obligation:
    Six-part discharge corresponding to (P1)..(P6); each grounded
    in (a) the per-dimension partial order defined in Annex E §AIMS §3.1 through §AIMS §3.5 and sec-5 IC-3, and (b) the structural
    match between spec values and the `ParamContract::OPTIMISTIC`
    Rust const at compiler/ori_arc/src/aims/contract/
    mod.rs lines 368-386.

    Part (P1) — Access bottom:

      Access is a 2-element chain `Borrowed < Owned` with join
      defined as `max` (Annex E §AIMS §3.1). Bottom of a
      finite chain under `max` join is the smallest element by
      definition; here that is `Borrowed`.

      The shipped const at mod.rs:369 reads:
        `access: AccessClass::Borrowed`
      which structurally matches the spec value. (P1) discharged.

    Part (P2) — Consumption bottom:

      Consumption is a 4-element chain
      `Dead < Linear < Affine < Unrestricted` with join `max`
      (Annex E §AIMS.2). Bottom is `Dead`.

      The shipped const at mod.rs:370 reads:
        `consumption: Consumption::Dead`
      structurally matching spec. (P2) discharged.

    Part (P3) — Cardinality bottom:

      Cardinality is a 3-element chain `Absent < Once < Many`
      with join `max` (Annex E §AIMS.3). Bottom is
      `Absent`.

      The shipped const at mod.rs:371 reads:
        `cardinality: Cardinality::Absent`
      structurally matching spec. (P3) discharged.

      Coherence side-condition (per Annex E §AIMS CN-1):
      `Cardinality = Absent ⟹ Consumption := Dead` is enforced
      by canonicalization. The shipped OPTIMISTIC const sets
      Consumption = Dead AND Cardinality = Absent simultaneously,
      so the (Dead, Absent) pair is already CN-1-canonical at
      initialization; no canonicalization round mutates the seed.

    Part (P4) — Locality bottom:

      Locality is a 5-element chain
      `BlockLocal < FunctionLocal < ArgEscaping < HeapEscaping
      < Unknown` with join `max` (Annex E §AIMS.5).
      Bottom is `BlockLocal`.

      The shipped const at mod.rs:374 reads:
        `locality_bound: Locality::BlockLocal`
      structurally matching spec. (P4) discharged.

      Coherence side-condition (per Annex E §AIMS CN-8):
      `Access = Borrowed ∧ Locality > FunctionLocal ⟹
      Locality := FunctionLocal` does NOT fire at initialization
      because Locality = BlockLocal < FunctionLocal. The seed is
      already CN-8-canonical; no canonicalization round mutates
      it. (CN-6's `Locality ≥ HeapEscaping ∧ Uniqueness = Unique
      ⟹ Uniqueness := MaybeShared` also does NOT fire because
      Locality = BlockLocal < HeapEscaping.)

    Part (P5) — Uniqueness bottom:

      Uniqueness is a 3-element chain
      `Unique < MaybeShared < Shared` with join `max`
      (Annex E §AIMS.4). Bottom is `Unique`.

      The shipped const at mod.rs:375 reads:
        `uniqueness: Uniqueness::Unique`
      structurally matching spec. (P5) discharged.

      Coherence side-condition (per Annex E §AIMS CN-6):
      already discharged in (P4) — Locality = BlockLocal is
      far below HeapEscaping, so the CN-6 implication is
      vacuously true at initialization.

    Part (P6) — `may_share` boolean bottom:

      `may_share` is a boolean joined by OR across call sites
      (Annex E §AIMS IC-3 "may_share(OR)"). Under OR-join,
      the unique minimum element is `false`.

      The shipped const at mod.rs:373 reads:
        `may_share: false`
      structurally matching spec. (P6) discharged.

      Coherence side-condition: `may_share` is orthogonal to the
      five lattice dimensions per Annex E §AIMS.5 note
      ("may_share = per-parameter property (orthogonal to
      Locality)"); no canonicalization rule mutates `may_share`
      based on other dimensions, so the seed survives CN-1
      through CN-8 unchanged.

    Per-dimension lattice height (informational, consumed by IC-7):
      Access height 1 (Borrowed → Owned)
      Consumption height 3 (Dead → Linear → Affine → Unrestricted)
      Cardinality height 2 (Absent → Once → Many)
      Locality height 4 (BlockLocal → FunctionLocal →
                            ArgEscaping → HeapEscaping → Unknown)
      Uniqueness height 2 (Unique → MaybeShared → Shared)
      may_share height 1 (false → true)
    Sum: 13 per-parameter promotion steps maximum before the
    five-dim+boolean tuple reaches the conservative top
    `(Owned, Unrestricted, Many, Unknown, Shared, true)`. IC-7
    convergence bound consumes this sum (`param_count × 13 + ...`
    per the spec formula; shipped formula uses `× 17` to absorb
    the three IC-4 return-flow dims and the target-vs-shipped
    `may_escape` field — see Target-vs-shipped axis carve-out
    above).

    Bottom-up SCC fixpoint soundness witness:

      IC-2 seeds the bottom; IC-3 joins component-wise toward
      conservative. Three soundness properties cascade:

      (S1) Seed is bottom of the product lattice.
        Per Birkhoff (Lattice Theory, 3rd ed., 1967, Theorem II.6)
        the product of finite chains under componentwise `max`
        has unique minimum element equal to the componentwise
        product of per-chain minima. Parts (P1)..(P6) verify each
        component is at its minimum; conjunction is therefore
        the product-lattice bottom.

      (S2) Monotone promotion preserves the partial order.
        Per Annex E §AIMS.8 L-6 transfer functions SHALL
        be monotone: `a ≤ b ⟹ f(a) ≤ f(b)`. Starting at bottom,
        every subsequent join via IC-3 produces a state
        `pc' ≥ pc` componentwise. Anti-monotone moves (downward
        flip on any dim) are LATTICE-PROHIBITED; CN-4 was removed
        from the canonicalization ruleset precisely because it
        anti-monotonically promoted `MaybeShared → Unique` on
        local+linear+unique states (Annex E §AIMS CN-4
        removal note).

      (S3) Bottom seed ensures fixpoint reaches the LEAST
      conservative bound consistent with observed call sites.
        Per Tarski (Pacific J. Math., 1955, "A lattice-theoretical
        fixpoint theorem") any monotone function on a complete
        lattice has a least fixpoint, and that least fixpoint is
        the supremum of the iterates starting from bottom. IC-2
        FIXES the start as bottom; IC-3 iterates monotonically;
        IC-7 (proven separately) bounds the iteration count at
        sum-of-heights. The converged ParamContract is therefore
        the least upper bound of observed call-site demands —
        any more-conservative seed (e.g., starting at TOP or at
        `Owned`/`Many`/`Shared`) would converge to a strictly
        weaker (more conservative) contract, missing legitimate
        elision opportunities.

    Coverage gate — corpus enumeration:

      The shipped const + seeding contract is exercised by the
      interprocedural test surface in
      compiler/ori_arc/src/aims/interprocedural/
      tests.rs and adjacent test modules. Each row below pins
      one or more (P1)..(P6) conjuncts:

        Row A: no_params — function with zero params;
                                     IC-2 vacuously satisfied
                                     (no seed needed)
        Row B: single_owned_param — caller passes Owned arg;
                                     IC-2 seeds Borrowed; IC-3
                                     promotes to Owned; (P1)
                                     monotonicity pin
        Row C: borrowed_dead_param — callee never uses param;
                                     IC-2 seeds Dead/Absent;
                                     IC-3 keeps Dead/Absent;
                                     (P2)+(P3) seed-survival pin
        Row D: locality_promote — callee escapes param to
                                     heap; IC-2 seeds BlockLocal;
                                     IC-3 promotes to
                                     HeapEscaping; (P4)
                                     monotonicity pin
        Row E: uniqueness_promote — caller passes MaybeShared
                                     arg; IC-2 seeds Unique;
                                     IC-3 promotes to
                                     MaybeShared; (P5)
                                     monotonicity pin
        Row F: may_share_promote — callee RcInc's param; IC-2
                                     seeds may_share=false;
                                     IC-3 promotes to true;
                                     (P6) OR-monotonicity pin
        Row G: recursive_scc — self-recursive function;
                                     SCC fixpoint iterates IC-2
                                     seed against own
                                     conservative use; (S2)+(S3)
                                     pin
        Row H: mutual_recursion — A calls B, B calls A; IC-1
                                     produces 1 SCC of size 2;
                                     IC-2 seeds both bottoms;
                                     IC-3 joins across the cycle;
                                     full IC-2+IC-3+IC-7
                                     interaction pin

      Coverage axes:
        (P1)..(P6) per-dim bottom:
          Rows B, C, D, E, F directly pin one dimension each;
          Row A vacuously covers all six
        (S1) product-lattice bottom:
          Row C is the dedicated pin — Borrowed+Dead+Absent+
          BlockLocal+Unique+may_share=false survives backward
          dataflow when callee never uses the param
        (S2) monotone promotion:
          Rows B, D, E, F each demonstrate one dimension's
          monotone advance from bottom under IC-3 join
        (S3) least-fixpoint:
          Rows G, H exercise multi-iteration SCC convergence;
          test asserts the converged contract is exactly the
          join of observed call-site demands, not a strictly
          weaker bound

    Negative-direction witness — anti-monotone seed rejected:

      Take Row B (single_owned_param). The correct IC-2 seed is
      `(Borrowed, Dead, Absent, BlockLocal, Unique, false)`.
      Suppose hypothetical implementer seeds instead with the
      CONSERVATIVE const at mod.rs:340 lines 340-361:
      `(Owned, Unrestricted, Many, Unknown, MaybeShared, true)`.

      Per L-6 monotonicity, every subsequent IC-3 join produces
      `pc' ≥ pc`. Starting at CONSERVATIVE, `pc'` STAYS at
      CONSERVATIVE across every iteration (CONSERVATIVE is the
      product-lattice top, fixed by `max`-join). The fixpoint
      converges immediately to CONSERVATIVE for EVERY parameter
      of EVERY function — regardless of actual call-site demand.

      Downstream consequence: DP-1 (`is_rc_needed`) evaluates
      `access = Owned ∧ consumption ≠ Dead` → true for every
      param; RC inc/dec emitted at every call site. DP-2
      (`is_rc_dec_unnecessary`) evaluates
      `cardinality = Absent ∨ consumption = Dead` → false for
      every param; no dec elision. The AIMS mission ("RC rare,
      not RC ops faster" per Annex E §AIMS §1 + Annex E §AIMS
      Mission) collapses — every RC op survives to emitted IR
      because the lattice can no longer prove any dim is below
      conservative.

      Tarski's least-fixpoint theorem (cited in S3) is the
      formal reason this fails: anti-monotone (or already-top)
      seeds violate the precondition that the iteration sequence
      starts AT or BELOW the desired least fixpoint. IC-2's
      most-optimistic seed is the soundness foundation IC-3 +
      IC-7 build on; weakening it weakens every downstream RC
      elision predicate.

    Negative-direction witness — wrong-dimension seed rejected:

      Take Row C (borrowed_dead_param). Suppose hypothetical
      implementer seeds Consumption = Linear instead of Dead.
      Per CN-1 (Annex E §AIMS): `Cardinality = Absent ⟹
      Consumption := Dead`. The canonicalization round overwrites
      the wrong seed back to Dead — observable behavior IS
      preserved at this scale, but the round-trip violates the
      "seed is already canonical" invariant (P3 coherence
      side-condition above), causing one extra canonicalization
      pass per function during fixpoint init.

      Conversely, suppose hypothetical implementer seeds
      Cardinality = Once but keeps Consumption = Dead. CN-1
      contrapositive: `Consumption = Dead ⟹ Cardinality :=
      Absent`. Canonicalization again overwrites — but this
      time the (Dead, Once) intermediate is incoherent per
      CN-1, and a buggy canonicalizer skipping CN-1 would
      permit it. The shipped const at mod.rs:368-386 sets BOTH
      simultaneously, so the (Dead, Absent) pair is already
      coherent — no canonicalization round can produce a
      different result.

    Negative-direction witness — `may_share=true` seed rejected:

      Take Row F (may_share_promote). Suppose hypothetical
      implementer seeds `may_share = true` instead of false.
      OR-join with any subsequent call-site demand keeps
      `may_share = true` — no observed demand can promote
      true → false (anti-monotone). Downstream consequence:
      DP-9 (`cow_mode`) evaluates `MaybeShared ∧ caller may
      have RcInc'd` for every param; static-unique fast path
      via `IC-3 ParamContract.uniqueness = Unique ⟹ StaticUnique`
      becomes unreachable for any parameter, because the
      converged `may_share = true` poisons the freshness
      argument.

      The `may_share = false` seed at mod.rs:373 is therefore
      load-bearing for the entire COW fast-path infrastructure;
      promoting it ELSEWHERE (e.g., in CN-* canonicalization)
      would require co-evolving DP-9 + RL-30 neutral access-fact
      derivation. The cleanest discipline is IC-2's seed at
      OR-identity, IC-3's monotone promotion via observed
      call-site evidence only.

    IC-2 has no upstream dependencies on AIMS contract layer:

      IC-2 consumes the CallGraph (via IC-1's topological
      ordering) and produces ParamContract seeds. It reads NO
      AimsStateMap, NO per-variable lattice state, NO prior
      ParamContract from any other function (the OPTIMISTIC const
      is hardcoded). The dependency chain at the proof-obligation
      level is acyclic:
        IC-1 --> IC-2 (parameter contract seeding per function)
        IC-2 --> IC-3 (parameter contract componentwise join)
        IC-2 --> IC-4 (return contract structural extraction)
        IC-2 --> IC-5 (effect summary derivation)

      IC-2 is the leaf of this dependency sub-tree (IC-1 is the
      leaf of the FULL tree, but IC-2 has no AIMS-layer parent).

