                           American Mathematical Society Colloquium
                           Publications, vol. XXV, 1967, Theorem
                           II.6 (product lattice has componentwise
                           minimum); Tarski, A., "A lattice-
                           theoretical fixpoint theorem and its
                           applications", Pacific Journal of
                           Mathematics, vol. 5, no. 2, pp. 285-309,
                           1955 (least fixpoint of monotone function
                           on complete lattice equals supremum of
                           bottom-iterates)
      complexity: O(1) per parameter — single struct-literal
                           emission
      determinism: deterministic; the `OPTIMISTIC` const is
                           compile-time-fixed across all targets
                           and all compilation sessions (deterministic
                           query contract)
      reference impl: `ParamContract::OPTIMISTIC` const at
                           compiler/ori_arc/src/aims/
                           contract/mod.rs lines 368-386; consumed
                           by ori_arc::aims::interprocedural::
                           analyze_program at SCC-entry seeding
      cross-language Lean 4 src/Lean/Compiler/IR/Borrow.lean
      prior art: seeds borrow inference parameters at
                           `Borrowed` (the analogue of Ori's IC-2
                           Access dim bottom); Lean's fixpoint
                           promotes to `Owned` based on demand
                           evidence, identical bottom-up monotone
                           shape to IC-2+IC-3

    Engines dispatched:
      interprocedural_summary (PRIMARY — emits the OPTIMISTIC
        seed for every parameter of every function in every SCC
        produced by IC-1; the verifier checks all six conjuncts
        (P1)..(P6) plus side-conditions:
          - (P1) AccessClass::Borrowed structural equality
          - (P2) Consumption::Dead structural equality
          - (P3) Cardinality::Absent structural equality +
            CN-1 coherence with (P2)
          - (P4) Locality::BlockLocal structural equality +
            CN-8 vacuous-implication check + CN-6 vacuous-
            implication check
          - (P5) Uniqueness::Unique structural equality
          - (P6) may_share=false structural equality + OR-
            identity check
        emits Fail on any divergence from the spec values OR
        on any CN-* coherence violation surfaced by the seed)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_06 interprocedural_summary engine discharges IC-2 via six-conjunct verification ((P1) Borrowed access + (P2) Dead consumption + (P3) Absent cardinality + (P4) BlockLocal locality + (P5) Unique uniqueness + (P6) may_share=false) plus three cascading soundness properties ((S1) product-lattice bottom + (S2) monotone promotion + (S3) Tarski least-fixpoint reachability) over an 8-test corpus covering zero-param / single-dim-promotion / multi-dim-promotion / recursive-SCC / mutual-recursion cases; algorithm soundness inherited from Birkhoff 1967 Theorem II.6 (product lattice minimum) + Tarski 1955 (least-fixpoint of monotone function); shipped engine `ParamContract::OPTIMISTIC` const at compiler/ori_arc/src/aims/contract/mod.rs lines 368-386 emits the seed in O(1) per parameter, deterministically across all targets (deterministic query contract); target-vs-shipped axis carve-out (`may_escape` legacy field initialized false, IC-4 return-flow fields initialized to None/false) preserves spec conformance on the 5 dims + may_share enumerated in Annex E §AIMS IC-2
